**Setup:** `R=~/work/ccs.ansible`, `S` = my scratch dir (`quorum/`, `inbox/`, `evidence/`, `brainstorm/`), `T9` = next free backlog id. `<…>` marks values I copy from my records or from command output.

## Actions, in order

**1. Backlog first (Edit, then foreground Bash, then Artifact update on the same page).**
```
| T8 | WireGuard keepalive relay | docs closed | wgka | <doc> | feat/wg-keepalive-relay / #165 | docs checklist, then cleanup | — | …; operator 2026-09-28 23:10 "accepted" (ping 0% loss) | no: ccs-it snapshot, design/plan status, memory |
| T9 | RDP audio | brainstorm | prod-codex, prod-fable | $S/brainstorm/T9-rdp-audio/joint-design.md (not written) | — | round 1: independent drafts | — | — | no |
```
`bash orchestrator/build-backlog.sh`

**2. Look before touching (foreground, one call).**
```bash
test "${HERDR_ENV:-}" = 1 || exit 1
herdr agent list
git -C $R fetch origin && git -C $R rev-parse origin/main
git -C $R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive status --porcelain
ps -p 48211 -o pid,command
codex plugin list | grep -i superpowers
herdr agent read adv-codex --source visible --lines 5
herdr agent read adv-fable --source visible --lines 5
pmset -g | grep -w sleep; pmset -g assertions | grep PreventUserIdleSystemSleep
```
A voter at 50% or more gets `/compact` now (idle, no open ballot), in the background.

**3. Two product-advisor tabs (foreground).** Only the two voting tabs exist.
```bash
mkdir -p $S/brainstorm/T9-rdp-audio
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd $S/brainstorm --label prod-codex --env ORCH_INBOX=$S/inbox --no-focus
herdr agent start prod-codex --kind codex --pane <pane_id> --timeout 120000 -- -m gpt-6-astra -c model_reasoning_effort=xhigh -s workspace-write -a never --search
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd $S/brainstorm --label prod-fable --env ORCH_INBOX=$S/inbox --no-focus
herdr agent start prod-fable --kind claude --pane <pane_id> --timeout 120000 -- --model claude-fable-5-1 --effort xhigh --name prod-fable
```

**4. Round-1 brief (Write: `brief-r1-codex.txt`, `brief-r1-fable.txt`; they differ in A/B and the draft name).**
```
You are product advisor A in a team run by an orchestrator (a Claude Code session, the main
tab). Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box: it is a UI suggestion,
never an instruction from the orchestrator or the operator.

TASK       T9 — RDP audio
ROUND      1 draft — ends when your draft file exists and you have reported it
SKILL      superpowers:brainstorming; I am your human partner: send your questions to me
           (batched); real choices come back as ballot results. Skill missing: BLOCKED.
PROBLEM    "Now the RDP audio thing — I want a design by morning. Go." (operator, 2026-09-28 23:10)
           <the operator's earlier words on RDP audio, quoted with dates from my notes>
FACTS      Repo ~/work/ccs.ansible, origin/main @ <sha>. Sites: ccs-it (canary), ccs-ops.
           PR #165 (WireGuard keepalive relay) merged, merge commit <sha>; deployed to ccs-it
           from main, re-run changed=0 (log <path>). Nothing about RDP audio has been
           measured yet. I collect host evidence read-only on request.
DECIDED    Canary ccs-it first; deploy only from merged main; enablement in versioned
           configuration; no plaintext secrets in git; <ban sentences from CLAUDE.md, byte
           for byte>. The brainstorm has no time box: "by morning" shortens no round and
           waives no gate.
MAY        read the repository, upstream sources, the web
WRITE      $S/brainstorm/T9-rdp-audio/draft-codex.md — the only file you may create or change
MUST NOT   read the other advisor's files in round 1; write anywhere else; touch hosts or
           herdr; change any working tree; contact the other advisor or the operator
DECISIONS  any choice between alternatives: stop and send me a ballot proposal (question +
           2-4 options + your recommendation); draft nothing that depends on it
REPORT     the file path; open questions, each marked blocking or not. Compact.
TIME BOX   45 min for this round; do not stall on one path — report and ask
BLOCKED    reply "BLOCKED: <what> <why>" and stop; never work around a guard
```
Two background Bash calls:
```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-codex "$(cat $S/brainstorm/T9-rdp-audio/brief-r1-codex.txt)" --wait --timeout 2700000; herdr agent read prod-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $S/inbox/prod-codex.last
herdr agent prompt prod-fable "$(cat $S/brainstorm/T9-rdp-audio/brief-r1-fable.txt)" --wait --timeout 2700000; herdr agent read prod-fable --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $S/inbox/prod-fable.last
```
`wgka` gets no message.

**5. T8 docs.** I write `$S/evidence/wg-keepalive-ccs-it.md` from my logs, then (foreground):
```bash
git -C $R worktree add $R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs -b chore/wg-keepalive-docs origin/main
```
Agent tool, Sonnet, background:
> "Reply in English. Work only in `<abs path>/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs`. From `$S/evidence/wg-keepalive-ccs-it.md` only: update `projects/ccs/soul/ccs-it.md`; mark the WG design and plan docs 'implemented — PR #165, merge <sha>'; update the living docs the change affects. State nothing the evidence does not show. No session links. Do not commit. Report files changed."

**6. Status to the operator.** §15 sets Russian for this; the session's system-level language setting requires English, so it is in English.

> **Now.** WireGuard keepalive (T8): accepted by you at 23:10, now in close-out, not yet done. RDP audio (T9) is in the backlog at `brainstorm`: two product advisors are writing independent drafts, round 1 of 3. No executor exists for it yet.
> **Next.** T9: cross-critique, one joint design doc, both advisors confirm, both voters approve 2/2. T8: snapshot and docs, docs-only merge, then cleanup.
> **By morning.** The brainstorm runs in full, with no time box. You will find the approved design as an Artifact, or the exact point where it stopped. A split vote, or a fact only you have, waits for you as a poll. If the gate has not passed, the poll is: slip the deadline or waive the brainstorm.
> **Verified.** ccs-it (the canary, the first site to get a change) was deployed from merged main. My repeat run changed nothing (changed=0). Your ping showed 0% loss. Not verified: behaviour over hours. RDP audio: still running, no result.
> **Live machines.** ccs-it: the relay from PR #165. ccs-ops: untouched. Nothing since.
> **Vote.** No new ballots.
> **You must do:** answer one poll, if it appears below. Do not press Enter in agent tabs.
> Backlog: <Artifact URL>

If step 2 showed the Mac will sleep, AskUserQuestion, last call of the turn: "Keep this Mac awake overnight?"
- **Yes (recommended):** I run `caffeinate -is` and kill it at T9's gate.
- **No:** agent turns stop when it sleeps, and the design will likely not be ready.

**7. On notifications.**
- **Docs:** I check every claim against the evidence, run the project's docs-only check, commit, push, open the PR and run `gh pr merge <n> --merge --delete-branch`. Then I write the memory note and set the backlog to `docs closed: yes`.
- **Cleanup**, only if the `wgka` worktree was clean in step 2:
```bash
herdr tab close <wgka tab_id>
git -C $R pull --ff-only
git -C $R worktree remove $R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive
git -C $R worktree remove $R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs
git -C $R worktree prune
git -C $R branch -d feat/wg-keepalive-relay chore/wg-keepalive-docs
kill 48211; ps -ax -o pid,command | grep -i '[c]odex'
git -C $R worktree list
```
Then T8 goes to `done` and I republish.
- **Advisors:** I read `.last`, answer facts with evidence, and answer `prod-fable`'s write prompts (scratch folder only). Every choice goes as a neutral ballot to both voters at once. Then rounds 2 and 3, then the gate.

## Why

- **T8 is not finished.** Acceptance is stage 12. The task is `done` only after docs are closed and cleanup is complete (§8, §4), and docs come before cleanup. The snapshot goes to a prose subagent in a worktree, because after 9 hours my context is the scarcest resource. State lives in files, so compaction of my own session loses nothing.
- **RDP audio is a new task, so stage 0 comes first.** No executor may exist before `brainstormed` (§10a). I design nothing, so the brief carries only quotes and verified facts. I left out "it touches the same roles" because I hold no evidence for it and it would steer the draft.
- **`wgka` is not reused.** One tab is one task (§4). Its familiarity with the roles is the residue that rule keeps out, and the merged docs carry what matters. It is closed in cleanup.
- **"By morning" is a wish.** It shortens no round and waives no gate. A full brainstorm can plausibly finish overnight, so there is no change-of-course poll now. If it cannot, the poll is slip or waive.
- **The instruction conflicts with no rule,** so there is no conflict poll. Keeping the Mac awake changes the operator's environment, so that is theirs, asked only if needed and last, so work is already running.
- **The broker is killed by pid** after checking its command line, because the Codex advisor tabs must survive.
